            <div xml:id="d388">

                <pb facs="0546" n="450" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg450"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.00/25080a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Summerlin</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-07-08T16:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 8, 1921—4
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>101. Whereas the consul at Tampico reported on July 1 [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >June 30</hi>] that he feared anti-American outbreaks because of the
                    unemployment growing out of the cessation of oil shipments, orders were issued
                    for warships to proceed to that port. Since the fears were <pb facs="0547"
                        n="451" xml:id="pg451"/> shown to be baseless, and the lives and property of
                    American citizens do not appear now to be endangered, the vessels have been
                    ordered to leave that port.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
